name: delta-is-change-since-last-sample
why: delta(x) is x minus the previous sample; the first sample has no prior, so it emits nothing. 10,20,35 → t2=20-10=10, t3=35-20=15.
expr: delta(nodeA.price)
keys: nodeA.price
resolve: LOCF
--- LOG ---
---
#00:00:01.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 1
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 10.0}
---
#00:00:02.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 2
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 20.0}
---
#00:00:03.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 3
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 35.0}
--- EXPECT ---
2 => 10.0
3 => 15.0
